        SET VERIFY=(NOPROCEDURE, IMAGE)

        SET NOVERIFY
2 WORKING_SET
    The SET WORKING_SET command changes the current process's working set
    values, within the quota and extent it was authorized when it was
    created (SHOW WORKING_SET shows them).  A value above its authorized
    bound is set to the bound, and the command then reports the values,
    as /LOG does.  The current limit is set to the new default at once
    (DCL runs between images).  With paging on (HELP CONFIG KEYS,
    vax.sysgen.paging.enable), a smaller limit takes the oldest pages out
    of the working set.

    Syntax:

        SET WORKING_SET [/LIMIT=n] [/QUOTA=n] [/EXTENT=n] [/[NO]ADJUST]
                        [/[NO]LOG]

    Qualifiers:

        /LIMIT=n        The default working set, in pages: the limit each
                        image starts with, and goes back to at its exit.
                        A value above the quota raises the quota too.
        /QUOTA=n        The working set quota: the most an image's
                        $ADJWSL can count on.  At most the authorized
                        quota and the extent.
        /EXTENT=n       The working set extent: the most $ADJWSL can
                        reach.  At most the authorized extent, and more
                        than the SYSGEN parameter MINWSCNT.  A smaller
                        extent brings the quota and limit down with it.
        /[NO]ADJUST     Whether the system may adjust the working set by
                        itself.  govax remembers and shows the setting,
                        but has no automatic adjustment.
        /[NO]LOG        Report the new values (/NOLOG is the default).

    Example:

        $ SET WORKING_SET/QUOTA=5000
        %SET-I-NEWLIMS, new working set:  Limit = 512  Quota = 1024  Extent = 16400
